      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1820, Arkansas set aside the springs as a reservation, and in 1832 President Jackson signed the act that made Hot Springs National Park the oldest U.S. park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
